WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
2017.

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.700
China is the largest source
of the goods the US imports:

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:11.270
505.6 billion dollars,
21.6 per cent of the total.

4
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.770
2023.

5
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:17.430
Mexico overtakes it, at
475.6 billion dollars.

6
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.910
China: 427.2 billion.

7
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:26.370
In 2024, Mexico's figure
reaches 505.9 billion.

8
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.990
So is the world un-globalizing?

9
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.710
Is world trade collapsing?

10
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.470
Or is it rebuilding for resilience?

11
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.630
In this mission, you'll meet
re-shoring and its relatives,

12
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.870
and test the evidence, from chip factories
to a sports brand that changed its

13
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:41.850
mind.

14
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.310
Then you'll see how crowd-sourcing, cyber
defence and smart borders manage flows

15
00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.290
of data and people.

16
00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.470
Your mission: decide whether
the world is un-globalizing,

17
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.790
or rebuilding for resilience.
